+# Veterinarian Search Is Narrowed to Admit Directory Filtering
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined searching for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian. It was derived from observed absence during the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey. A request to filter the veterinarian directory by specialty falls inside that row as written.
+
+The owner decided the row at intake on 2026-10-30: "free-text veterinarian search stays out of scope, but filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows is in." The same intake states that the filter is a URL contract only, and that a visible control may come as a follow-up request.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Keep NG-9 as written.** Rejected: the owner decided otherwise.
+2. **Remove NG-9.** Rejected: the owner keeps free-text veterinarian search out of scope, and the row's pet and visit clauses are untouched.
+3. **Narrow NG-9 and declare the page control out of scope** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-9 keeps declining free-text veterinarian search and every search for a pet or a visit. Filtering the veterinarian directory by an attribute it already shows is in scope.
+
+NG-10 declares a form, dropdown, or other page control for the filter out of scope. The decline is the owner's for this request, with a follow-up left open.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- NG-9 leaves the open provenance consultation; the Non-Goals preamble names it decided. NG-10 was decided when it was added.
+- Only the specialty filter is built. Filtering by another attribute the directory shows needs its own request.
+- A visible control arrives only through a follow-up request that decides NG-10.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9, NG-10
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row, the new row, and the updated preamble.
+- [PRD Veterinarian directory](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the filter this narrowing admits.
